he `/find-existing <thing>` slash command before building anything new.\n\n## Output format\n\nEnd with a 5-line \"first PR checklist\" tailored to their area:\n1. Pull latest `main`, branch as `feat/<topic>` or `fix/<topic>`.\n2. Read the rule file and matching engineer subagent.\n3. Use `/find-existing` before writing new utilities.\n4. Run the area's test command before committing.\n5. Open PR with the template in `.cursor/rules/pr-workflow.mdc`.\n\nKeep total response under ~80 lines. This is an orientation, not a manual.","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QdKpmxWbKUHEUAsoaJ1pey","duration_ms":39}
[2026-05-09 16:00:19] {"session_id":"a4497b75-5f05-4051-b635-c0ef344aff1b","transcript_path":"/Users/sarabjyotsingh/.claude/projects/-Users-sarabjyotsingh-IdeaProjects-pulse/a4497b75-5f05-4051-b635-c0ef344aff1b.jsonl","cwd":"/Users/sarabjyotsingh/IdeaProjects/pulse","permission_mode":"default","effort":{"level":"xhigh"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Write","tool_input":{"file_path":"/Users/sarabjyotsingh/IdeaProjects/pulse/.claude/TESTING.md","content":"# Claude Code harness — manual test plan\n\nRun these in a **fresh `claude` session** at the repo root. Mark pass/fail in the checkboxes. If anything fails, capture the prompt + observed output and bring it back.\n\n> All hooks currently live in `.claude/settings.local.json` (personal). They are not yet team-shared in `.claude/settings.json`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Slash command discovery\n\n- [ ] **Setup:** at the prompt, type `/` (don't send).\n- [ ] **Expect:** `find-existing` and `onboard` appear in the autocomplete list, alongside the ported cursor commands (`build-backend`, `review-my-changes`, etc.).\n- **If fails:** symlink `.claude/commands → ../.cursor/commands` is broken. `ls -la .claude/commands` should show the symlink.\n\n## 2. /onboard backend\n\n- [ ] **Run:** `/onboard backend`\n- [ ] **Expect:** ~80-line response covering: 1-paragraph orientation, backend rule + subagent pointer, top 3–5 backend slash commands, build/test command, safety rules, 5-line first-PR checklist.\n- [ ] **Quality bar:** would a brand-new backend engineer find this useful? If it reads generic, the `description` lines in `.cursor/rules/`/`.cursor/agents/` aren't pulling their weight — note which sections felt thin.\n\n## 3. block-secrets-in-commands (PreToolUse Bash)\n\n- [ ] **Run:** ask claude to \"set my GitHub token by exporting `GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa` so I can use gh\".\n- [ ] **Expect:** the bash tool call is denied with a message about secret pattern `ghp_[a-zA-Z0-9]{36}`. Claude should suggest using `.env` instead.\n- **If fails:** check that `.claude/hooks/block-secrets-in-commands.sh` is executable (`ls -l`) and that `settings.local.json` has the PreToolUse hook entry.\n\n## 4. block-sensitive-reads (PreToolUse Read)\n\n- [ ] **Run:** \"Read `deploy/.env` and tell me what's in it.\"\n- [ ] **Expect:** the Read tool call is denied with a message pointing at `.env.example`.\n- [ ] **Counter-test:** \"Read `deploy/.env.example`\" — should succeed (template, not blocked).\n\n## 5. block-destructive (PreToolUse Bash, ask)\n\n- [ ] **Run:** \"Run `mysql -e 'DROP TABLE users'` in the backend container.\"\n- [ ] **Expect:** claude tries the bash, the harness prompts you with the destructive-pattern message and waits for your approval.\n- [ ] **You decide:** allow once = it runs. Deny = it shouldn't retry.\n\n## 6. /find-existing\n\n- [ ] **Run:** `/find-existing date formatting helper for relative time`\n- [ ] **Expect:** searches `pulse-ui/src/helpers/`, `pulse-ui/src/utils/`, etc.; returns at least one or two matches with `path:line` references; ends with an opinionated reuse / extend / build-new recommendation.\n- [ ] **Counter-test:** `/find-existing thing-that-definitely-does-not-exist-xyz` — should explicitly say \"no existing implementation found\".\n\n## 7. backend-engineer subagent auto-invoke\n\n- [ ] **Run:** \"Add a new endpoint to pulse-server that returns the count of unresolved alerts for a project.\"\n- [ ] **Expect:** claude either spawns the `backend-engineer` subagent via the Agent tool, or its plan visibly references the conventions in `.cursor/agents/backend-engineer.md` (Service interface + impl, ServiceError enum, RxJava3 types, MapStruct mapper, Queries.java for SQL).\n- **If fails:** claude isn't auto-invoking — the agent's `description` frontmatter may need to be more aggressive (e.g. start with \"Use proactively when…\").\n\n## 8. auto-format (PostToolUse Edit|Write)\n\n- [ ] **Run:** \"Add a console.log line at the top of `pulse-ui/src/App.tsx`.\"\n- [ ] **After:** run `git diff pulse-ui/src/App.tsx` — formatting (quotes, spacing) should match the file's existing prettier conventions, even if claude wrote it differently.\n- [ ] **Audit log check:** `tail -3 .claude/hooks/state/audit.log` should show a `PostToolUse` entry for the Edit.\n\n## 9. verify-on-stop (Stop)\n\n- [ ] **Run:** \"Edit `pulse-ui/src/App.tsx` and add the line `const x: string = 42;` somewhere — that's a deliberate type error.\"\n- [ ] **Expect:** claude makes the edit, then on stop, `verify-on-stop.sh` runs `tsc --noEmit`, fails, and `decision: block` causes claude to continue and fix the error before truly stopping.\n- [ ] **Loop guard:** confirm it doesn't fire forever — `stop_hook_active` should kick in on the second pass.\n- **If fails:** verify-on-stop probably ran `tsc` successfully (cached node_modules?) or claude isn't honoring the `decision: block` JSON.\n\n## 10. session-init (SessionStart)\n\n- [ ] **Setup:** open a fresh `claude` session at the repo root.\n- [ ] **First prompt:** \"What branch am I on and what services are running?\"\n- [ ] **Expect:** claude knows the current git branch, dirty file count, recent commits, and pulse-* docker container names — without running any tools to figure it out (because session-init injected them as additionalContext).\n\n## 11. audit log\n\n- [ ] **After running tests 3–9:** `wc -l .claude/hooks/state/audit.log`\n- [ ] **Expect:** dozens of entries, JSON-per-line, timestamps in order.\n- [ ] **Rotation sanity:** size <5MB. If approaching, `audit.log.old` should appear.\n\n---\n\n## Failure triage\n\n| Symptom | First place to look |\n|---|---|\n| Slash command missing | `ls -la .claude/commands` (symlink intact?) |\n| Hook never fires | `.claude/settings.local.json` `hooks` block — matcher wrong? |\n| Hook crashes silently | `.claude/hooks/state/audit.log`; or run hook standalone with a saved JSON input |\n| Subagent doesn't auto-invoke | `description` front